     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi folks,<div><br>Just a quick follow up, I updated the resources and some structuring of the github repo for this talk (<a href=\"https://github.com/ryanpeek/rmarkdown_notebook_demo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/ryanpeek/rmarkdown_notebook_demo&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467146184000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3P0yoJvm4-hyJBUZQYaWEw\">https://github.com/ryanpeek/rmarkdown_notebook_demo</a>), please take a look/update.</div><div><br></div><div>The talk will be here for viewing in perpetuity: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Fgx229pWi8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v%3D_Fgx229pWi8&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467146184000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ni7usQtUGrogoDFQof7v9\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Fgx229pWi8</a></div><div><br></div><div>Also in particular someone kindly pointed out a really nice website that might help with making the transition to writing in a plain-text/markdown format. It&#39;s really nice (though long) perspective and I think worth checking out (<b><a href=\"http://plain-text.co/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plain-text.co/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467146184000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0OfZZoo3g2TzwtmlUZYS6L\">http://plain-text.co/</a></b>).</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Adios,</div><div><br></div><div>R</div><div><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(